Not modified, worked around instead: on Windows, scripts/office/soffice.py
probes socket.AF_UNIX, which does not exist there, and recalc.py then aborts.
tools/office-check/run_recalc.py (our code, not part of this vendored set)
patches that probe in-process before calling the unmodified recalc.main().

